================================================================================================================
L153 -- can anything DELIVER a sound speed that grows with a?  Two theorems, three obstructions, one realization
================================================================================================================

================================================================================================================
PART 0 -- THE BAROTROPIC DICTIONARY: 'c_s^2 grows with a' is IDENTICALLY 'c_s^2 falls with rho'.
================================================================================================================
      continuity            dln rho / dln a   =  -3 (1 + w)
      barotropic chain rule dln c_s^2 / dln a =  -3 (1 + w) * dln c_s^2 / dln rho  =  3 (1 + w) nu

      so                    p  ==  dln c_s^2/dln a  =  3*nu*(w + 1)          with nu = -dln c_s^2/dln rho

      THE DENSITY-TIME DUALITY.  For a barotropic fluid c_s^2 is a function of rho ALONE.  Demanding
      that c_s^2 grow with the scale factor is therefore the SAME demand as that c_s^2 fall with density.
      But a galaxy IS a region of high density.  The property that lets the fluid evade the L125 lemma
      cosmologically is the property that makes it soft exactly where the galaxy gate needs it stiff.
      Concretely: the fluid inside a present-day structure of overdensity Delta has EXACTLY the sound
      speed the universe had at a = (1+Delta)^{-1/3}.  A galaxy is a time machine for a barotropic fluid.
  [PASS] DUAL-1  the barotropic dictionary is an identity, not a model: p = dln c_s^2/dln a = 3(1+w) nu with nu = -dln c_s^2/dln rho.  Growth in time and softening with density are the SAME statement, so the cosmological evasion and the galaxy gate are not independent -- they read the same function   (p = 3(1+w)nu  identically; a structure of overdensity Delta sees c_s^2 at a=(1+Delta)^(-1/3))

================================================================================================================
PART 1 -- THEOREM A (growth ceiling): a barotropic fluid whose sound speed grows obeys c_s^2 <= w, hence p < 3(1+w).
================================================================================================================
  Hypotheses.  (H1) barotropic: P = P(rho).  (H2) no gradient instability: c_s^2 = P'(rho) >= 0.
  (H3) the growth condition: c_s^2 non-increasing in rho (equivalently P concave).  (H4) the null energy
  condition rho + P >= 0 holds down to rho -> 0, which forces P(0) >= 0.

  Proof.  By (H3), c_s^2(rho) <= c_s^2(rho') for every rho' <= rho, so
        c_s^2(rho) * rho  =  integral_0^rho c_s^2(rho) drho'  <=  integral_0^rho c_s^2(rho') drho'
                          =  P(rho) - P(0)  <=  P(rho)          [by (H4)]
  hence  c_s^2 <= P/rho = w.  QED.

      power-law family  P = A rho^Gamma :   c_s^2 = A*Gamma*rho**(Gamma - 1),   w = A*rho**(Gamma - 1),   c_s^2/w = Gamma
                                            nu = -dln c_s^2/dln rho = 1 - Gamma  =  1 - Gamma
                                            p  = 3(1+w) nu  ->  3(1-Gamma) for w << 1
  [PASS] THMA-1  on the power-law family the theorem is an identity: c_s^2/w = Gamma, and (H2) c_s^2 >= 0 with A > 0 forces Gamma > 0, so c_s^2 <= w exactly when Gamma <= 1 -- which is exactly the growth condition nu = 1 - Gamma >= 0.  Growth and c_s^2 <= w are the same constraint   (c_s^2/w = Gamma;  nu = 1 - Gamma;  growth (nu>0) <=> Gamma<1 <=> c_s^2 < w)

      p = 3(1 - Gamma)  =>  Gamma = 1 - p/3,  and  w/c_s^2 = 1/Gamma = -3/(p - 3) = 3/(3-p).
      Gamma > 0 (no gradient instability) is therefore  p < 3  STRICTLY, and the price of approaching the
      ceiling is w/c_s^2 = 3/(3-p), which DIVERGES as p -> 3.

           p    Gamma    w/c_s^2    w_0 for c_s(1)=207 km/s
        0.00   1.0000      1.000                  4.768e-07
        1.00   0.6667      1.500                  7.151e-07
        2.00   0.3333      3.000                  1.430e-06
        2.50   0.1667      6.000                  2.861e-06
        2.90   0.0333     30.000                  1.430e-05
        2.99   0.0033    300.000                  1.430e-04
        3.00   0.0000   infinite     FORBIDDEN (c_s^2 <= 0)
  [PASS] THMA-2  THEOREM A, sharp form.  For a barotropic fluid with c_s^2 >= 0, growing with a, and NEC-safe at low density, c_s^2 <= w.  On the power-law family this is p < 3(1+w), i.e. p < 3 to the accuracy that matters, and the cost of approaching the ceiling is w/c_s^2 = 3/(3-p) -> infinity.  There is NO barotropic fluid with p >= 3   (p < 3 strictly;  w/c_s^2 = 3/(3-p);  p=2.9 costs w = 10 c_s^2, p=2.99 costs w = 100 c_s^2)

================================================================================================================
PART 2 -- THEOREM B (climb bound): how deep a well can a barotropic fluid climb, from its own history?
================================================================================================================
  Hydrostatic equilibrium of a barotropic fluid:  dP/dr = -rho dPhi/dr, i.e.  c_s^2(rho) drho/rho = -dPhi.
  Integrating from the cosmic mean rho_bar (where Phi = Phi_ref) inward to arbitrarily high density:

        Delta_Phi_max  =  integral_{rho_bar}^{infinity} c_s^2(rho) dln rho

  and, by the DENSITY-TIME DUALITY of PART 0 (dln rho = -3 dln a along the cosmological trajectory),

        Delta_Phi_max  =  3 * integral_0^1 c_s^2(a) dln a.

  THE FLUID CAN CLIMB EXACTLY THREE TIMES ITS OWN LOG-INTEGRATED COSMOLOGICAL SOUND-SPEED HISTORY.
  For the power-law family this evaluates in closed form:

        3 * integral_{-inf}^{0} c_s^2(1) e^{p lna} dlna  =  3*c_s2/p     (converges only for p > 0)
  [PASS] THMB-1  THEOREM B: the maximum potential depth a barotropic fluid can climb from the cosmic mean is Delta_Phi_max = integral c_s^2 dln rho = 3 * integral_0^1 c_s^2(a) dln a, which for the power-law family is exactly 3 c_s^2(1)/p.  A fluid that grows FASTER (larger p) can climb LESS -- the two requirements of the hybrid pull in opposite directions through one and the same function   (Delta_Phi_max = 3 c_s^2(1)/p;  isothermal (p=0) diverges, i.e. an isothermal fluid can climb any well)

  COROLLARY (no regular hydrostatic solution).  A MOND galaxy has Phi = v_c^2 ln r with UNBOUNDED depth
  as r -> 0.  For any p > 0, Delta_Phi_max is FINITE, so there is a finite radius
        r_crit  =  r_ref exp( -Delta_Phi_max / v_c^2 )  =  r_ref exp( -3 c_s^2(1) / (p v_c^2) )
  at which the hydrostatic density diverges as (r - r_crit)^{-3/p}.  Inside r_crit the fluid does not
  merely compress -- it CONDENSES, with no pressure support at all.  A fluid whose sound speed grows in
  time has NO pressure support beyond a finite well depth.

        c_s(1) | p=0.5    p=1      p=2      p=3         (r_crit in kpc, v_c=300 km/s, r_ref=3 Mpc)
           207 | 1.72e+02  7.19e+02  1.47e+03  1.86e+03
           400 | 6.99e-02  1.45e+01  2.08e+02  5.07e+02
           700 | 1.95e-11  2.42e-04  8.52e-01  1.30e+01
          1100 | 2.78e-32  9.13e-15  5.23e-06  4.35e-03
          1600 | 2.28e-71  2.61e-34  8.86e-16  1.33e-09
  [PASS] THMB-2  COROLLARY: for any p > 0 a barotropic fluid has a finite condensation radius inside every logarithmic (MOND) galaxy potential, r_crit = r_ref exp(-3 c_s^2(1)/(p v_c^2)), where the hydrostatic density diverges as (r-r_crit)^{-3/p} and the enclosed mass diverges.  Keeping r_crit below the rotation-curve region costs c_s^2(1) > (p/3) v_c^2 ln(r_ref/r) -- LINEAR in p   (v_c=300, p=1: c_s=207 km/s (the L152 galaxy minimum) condenses already at 719 kpc, i.e. the condensation front ENCLOSES the whole galaxy; pushing it below 1 kpc needs c_s > 1600 km/s (2.6e-34 kpc))

================================================================================================================
PART 3 -- THE OTHER MECHANISMS, each on its own terms.
================================================================================================================
  (b) FUZZY / ULTRALIGHT DARK MATTER.  The quantum-pressure dispersion is omega^2 = (hbar k^2/(2 m a^2))^2,
      so the effective propagation speed at fixed COMOVING k is  c_eff = hbar k/(2 m a)  --  proportional
      to 1/a, EXACTLY the decoupled scaling.  Hence p = -2, and the Jeans wavenumber is
        c_eff(a) = hbar*k/(2*a*m)     dln c_eff/dln a = -1   (i.e. p = -2)
        k_J(a) = 2*pi**(1/4)*G**(1/4)*a**(1/4)*sqrt(m)*rho0**(1/4)/sqrt(hbar)
        dln k_J/dln a = 1/4    (the textbook a^{1/4} of Hu-Barkana-Gruzinov 2000)
  [PASS] FDM-1  fuzzy / ultralight dark matter is a SECOND, independent instance of the velocity-ordering obstruction, not an escape from it.  Its quantum-pressure speed at fixed comoving k is hbar k/(2 m a), proportional to 1/a -- the same p = -2 as a decoupled particle -- and the Jeans wavenumber therefore goes as a^{1/4}, INCREASING: its clustering set grows in time, the wrong direction   (c_eff ~ 1/a  =>  p = -2;  k_J ~ a^(1/4) INCREASING (wrong direction, same as decoupled))

  (d) GHOST CONDENSATE.  At the shift-symmetric minimum P_X = 0, so c_s^2 = 0 at leading order and the
      dispersion is set by the higher-derivative term: omega^2 = k^4/(M^2 a^4).  The propagation speed at
      fixed comoving k is again k/(M a) -- proportional to 1/a, p = -2.  A THIRD instance of the same
      obstruction, with the same k^4 structure as fuzzy DM.  Additionally, a ghost condensate has a
      Jeans-like GRAVITATIONAL instability of its own (the programme's g03x), so it is not a candidate.
  [PASS] GC-1  a ghost condensate is a THIRD instance of the same obstruction: with P_X = 0 the leading dispersion is omega^2 = k^4/(M^2 a^4), so the propagation speed at fixed comoving k is k/(M a), again proportional to 1/a and again p = -2.  Every k^4 (higher-derivative) dispersion sits at p = -2, because k/a is a physical wavenumber   (omega^2 = k^4/M^2a^4  =>  c_eff = k/(Ma) ~ 1/a  =>  p = -2 (same corner as decoupled and fuzzy))

  (a) SHIFT-SYMMETRIC k-ESSENCE, P = X^n.  This is the barotropic case, and it is the one mechanism that
      DOES deliver a healthy, matter-like fluid with a finite sound speed:
        rho = 2 X P_X - P = X**n*(2*n - 1)          w = P/rho = 1/(2*n - 1)
        c_s^2 = P_X/(P_X + 2 X P_XX) = 1/(2*n - 1)     (equal to w EXACTLY: the THEOREM A bound is SATURATED)
        no-ghost / no-gradient-instability:  P_X + 2 X P_XX = X**(n - 1)*n*(2*n - 1) > 0 for n > 0, X > 0
        to realise a given c_s^2:  n = (c_s2 + 1)/(2*c_s2);  for c_s^2 = 4.76e-7 this is n = 1.050e+06
  [PASS] KESS-1  a POSITIVE result: shift-symmetric k-essence P = X^n realizes a healthy constant-sound-speed dark fluid exactly, with c_s^2 = w = 1/(2n-1), no ghost and no gradient instability for n > 0.  So p = 0 (which L152 showed threads both of L125's gates) IS realizable by an explicit Lagrangian -- the loophole is not merely a parameterisation   (P = X^n:  c_s^2 = w = 1/(2n-1) > 0, P_X + 2X P_XX = n(2n-1)X^(n-1) > 0 (healthy))

        BBN / stiff tail: the conserved shift charge gives rho proportional to a^{-6*n/(2*n - 1)} = a^{-3(1+c_s^2)}.
        For c_s^2 = 4.76e-7 the exponent is -3.0000014, not -6.  L123's 'generic a^-6 stiff tail' is
        the n = 1 (canonical, c_s^2 = 1) corner of this family; at small c_s^2 there is NO separate stiff
        branch and NO BBN problem.  This is a correction to L123 STIFF-1, in the loophole's favour.
  [PASS] KESS-2  CORRECTION TO L123.  L123's STIFF-1 says a finite-c_s shift-symmetric k-essence generically carries an a^-6 stiff tail with a ~24-order BBN tuning.  Quantified, the exponent is -3(1+c_s^2), which for the c_s^2 of interest (1e-6) is -3.000003, not -6.  The a^-6 tail is the canonical n = 1 (c_s^2 = 1) corner only.  The BBN objection does NOT apply to a slow dark fluid   (rho ~ a^-3(1+c_s^2) = a^-3.000001 for c_s^2 = 4.8e-7 -- no stiff branch, no BBN tail)

  (c) A DARK-SECTOR PHASE TRANSITION OR LATE-TIME HEATING (decay products, dark radiation drag, dark
      photon coupling).  Two independent obstructions, both quantitative:

        mean free path at the cosmic mean density with sigma/m = 1 cm^2/g (the Bullet-Cluster ceiling):
              lambda = 1/(rho sigma/m) = 1.25e+05 Mpc   -- vastly larger than the horizon.
        to be a HYDRODYNAMIC fluid on 1 Mpc at the cosmic mean density one needs
              sigma/m > 1.25e+05 cm^2/g,  i.e. 5.1 orders above the bound.
  [PASS] HEAT-1  a PARTICLE realization of GDM is excluded by the mean free path, independently of any heating history.  A sound speed is a hydrodynamic quantity: it requires lambda_mfp << the scale.  At the cosmic mean density, sigma/m = 1 cm^2/g (the Bullet-Cluster / halo-shape ceiling) gives lambda of order 1e5 Mpc; being a fluid on Mpc scales demands sigma/m ~ 1e5-1e6 cm^2/g, five to six orders above the bound.  Particles at the cosmic mean density FREE-STREAM -- and free-streaming is p = -2   (lambda(sigma/m=1) = 1.2e+05 Mpc; need sigma/m > 1.2e+05 cm^2/g (5.1 dex above the bound))

        And the ENERGY budget is NOT the obstruction, which is worth recording: raising the specific
        internal energy to c_s^2 ~ 5e-7 c^2 costs 5e-7 of the dark rest mass, i.e. Omega ~ 1e-7 -- far
        below any dark-radiation bound.  So heating fails on the MECHANISM (thermalization), not on the
        energy.  For DECAYING dark matter specifically: particles kicked at time t cool as a(t)/a
        afterwards (p = -2 again from the kick onward), and the UNDECAYED cold fraction still clusters
        in galaxies and still spends the L61 excess.  A short lifetime removes the cold fraction but
        then the kicked population has been cooling for a Hubble time.  No escape either way.
  [PASS] HEAT-2  the energy budget is explicitly NOT the obstruction (recorded so the kill is attributed to the right cause): heating the dark sector to c_s^2 ~ 5e-7 c^2 costs ~1e-6 of its rest mass, Omega ~ 1e-7 today, invisible to every dark-radiation bound.  Late heating dies on thermalization (HEAT-1) and on the surviving cold fraction, not on energetics   (Delta u / (rest mass) = 7.14e-07; Omega_extra ~ 1.9e-07 -- unconstrained)

================================================================================================================
PART 4 -- Q2: THE BACKGROUND COST.  Does a nonzero c_s^2 spoil the expansion history / BAO?
================================================================================================================
  A barotropic fluid with c_s^2 has w = c_s^2 * 3/(3-p) (THEOREM A), and w inherits the same time
  dependence, w(a) = w_0 a^p.  The background density then integrates to
        rho_d(a) = rho_d,0 a^-3 exp( -3 [w(a) - w_0] / p ),   so   rho_d(a)/rho_d^{CDM}(a) - 1  ~  3w_0/p
  at a = 1 and is exponentially smaller in the past.  Numbers for the L152 window:

          p         w_0   d rho_d/rho_d (a=1)   d E/E (z=0.5)   d D_C(z=1100)/D_C
       0.50   5.721e-07             3.433e-06       7.166e-07           5.393e-07
       1.00   7.151e-07             2.145e-06       3.657e-07           1.928e-07
       2.00   1.430e-06             2.145e-06       2.438e-07           9.113e-08
       2.90   1.430e-05             1.480e-05       1.167e-06           3.959e-07
  [PASS] BG-1  the BACKGROUND COST IS NIL, and this is reported as a NON-kill.  Across the whole L152 window the fluid's equation of state today is w_0 = 3 c_s^2/(3-p) < 1e-5, the dark density departs from a^-3 by < 1e-5, and the comoving distance to last scattering (hence theta_s, hence BAO calibration) shifts by < 1e-5 -- four orders below the measurement.  Task 3's 'this may be the actual kill' is answered: it is NOT.  The component is matter for every background observable   (worst of |d rho_d/rho_d|, |dE/E|, |dD_C/D_C| over p in [0.5, 2.9] = 1.48e-05)
  [PASS] BG-2  and the reason is structural, not numerical: THEOREM A ties w to c_s^2 by w = 3c_s^2/(3-p), and the galaxy gate only ever asks for c_s^2 of order (v_c/c)^2 ~ 1e-6.  A sound speed large enough to smooth a galaxy is automatically far too small to matter for the expansion history.  Background self-consistency can never be the obstruction in this class   (even at p = 2.9 (worst case) w_0 = 1.43e-05; the galaxy gate needs only c_s ~ v_c)

================================================================================================================
VERDICT
================================================================================================================

  PART 2 VERDICT -- the mechanism map.

  REALIZABLE (and healthy):
    * shift-symmetric k-essence P = X^n gives a constant-sound-speed dark fluid with c_s^2 = w = 1/(2n-1),
      no ghost, no gradient instability, and -- correcting L123's STIFF-1 -- rho proportional to
      a^{-3(1+c_s^2)} = a^-3.000003, NOT a^-6.  There is no BBN tail for a slow fluid.  So p = 0, which
      L152 showed threads both of L125's gates, is delivered by an explicit Lagrangian.

  BOUNDED (two theorems, both new here):
    * THEOREM A -- a barotropic fluid whose sound speed grows obeys c_s^2 <= w, hence p < 3 strictly, with
      the cost w/c_s^2 = 3/(3-p) diverging at the ceiling.  No barotropic fluid reaches p = 3.
    * THEOREM B -- such a fluid can climb a potential well of depth at most 3 * integral c_s^2 dln a, i.e.
      3 c_s^2(1)/p for a power law.  For any p > 0 that is FINITE, so a MOND logarithmic potential (which is
      unbounded) always has a condensation radius r_crit = r_ref exp(-3c_s^2(1)/(p v_c^2)) inside which the
      fluid has no pressure support at all.  Growing FASTER buys LESS galaxy protection: one function is
      being asked to do two opposite jobs.

  DEAD ON ARRIVAL (three separate instances of the SAME p = -2 obstruction):
    * fuzzy / ultralight DM: c_eff = hbar k/(2 m a) ~ 1/a, k_J ~ a^{1/4} INCREASING.  Wrong direction.
    * ghost condensate:      omega^2 = k^4/M^2a^4, c_eff = k/(M a) ~ 1/a.  Wrong direction.  (And it carries
                             its own gravitational instability.)
    * collisional particles / late heating: a sound speed is hydrodynamic and needs lambda_mfp << scale;
      at the cosmic mean density that costs sigma/m ~ 1e5-1e6 cm^2/g, five to six orders above the
      Bullet-Cluster bound.  Particles at the mean density free-stream, and free-streaming IS p = -2.
      The energy budget is NOT the problem (1e-6 of the rest mass); thermalization is.

  NOT THE OBSTRUCTION (reported as such, so nothing is mis-attributed):
    * the background.  w_0 = 3c_s^2/(3-p) < 1e-5 everywhere in the window; rho_d departs from a^-3 by
      < 1e-5; the distance to last scattering shifts by < 1e-5.  Task 3's candidate kill is answered NO.

  So the class of mechanisms narrows to exactly one live family: a BAROTROPIC fluid / shift-symmetric
  k-essence with 0 <= p < 3, plus the unbounded NON-barotropic case in which c_s^2 depends on something
  other than the local density.  L154 puts the first through the epochs between recombination and today.

